# Link: Real-Time Communication Platform

**Link** is a modern, full-stack real-time communication platform designed for seamless text, media, and video communication. It provides users with real-time messaging, temporary status updates, group conversations, and video calling through a scalable web architecture.

---

## Core Capabilities

### Instant Messaging

* Real-time text messaging
* Persistent chat history
* One-to-one conversations
* Group conversations
* Multimedia sharing
* Image, video, and document support
* Real-time message updates

### Ephemeral Stories

* Share temporary status updates
* Support for text and media-based statuses
* Status updates automatically expire after 24 hours
* View and manage status updates
* Privacy-aware status functionality

### WebRTC Video Calls

* Real-time audio and video communication
* One-to-one video calls
* Group video communication
* Mute and unmute microphone
* Enable and disable camera
* Real-time call signaling using Socket.io/WebSockets

### User Management

* JWT-based authentication
* User registration and login
* Custom user profiles
* Profile avatars
* User information management
* Contact search
* Group creation and management
* Add and remove group members

### Real-Time Notifications

* Incoming message notifications
* Call notifications
* Status update notifications
* Real-time communication using WebSockets

---

## Technical Stack

### Frontend

* React.js
* Tailwind CSS
* Vite
* Reusable UI components

### Backend

* Node.js
* Express.js
* REST APIs
* Middleware-based architecture

### Real-Time Communication

* Socket.io
* WebSockets
* WebRTC

### Database and Storage

* MongoDB
* MongoDB Atlas
* Multer for file uploads

### Authentication

* JSON Web Tokens (JWT)
* Authentication middleware

---

