## Application Architecture

```text
                    ┌─────────────────────┐
                    │       Client        │
                    │   React + Vite      │
                    └──────────┬──────────┘
                               │
                  REST API / WebSockets
                               │
                               ▼
                    ┌─────────────────────┐
                    │       Server        │
                    │ Node.js + Express   │
                    └───────┬─────┬───────┘
                            │     │
                 ┌──────────┘     └──────────┐
                 ▼                           ▼
        ┌─────────────────┐        ┌─────────────────┐
        │    MongoDB      │        │    Socket.io    │
        │    Database     │        │ Real-Time Layer │
        └─────────────────┘        └────────┬────────┘
                                            │
                                            ▼
                                      ┌─────────────┐
                                      │   WebRTC    │
                                      │ Video Calls │
                                      └─────────────┘
```

---

## Real-Time Features

Link uses real-time communication technologies to provide an interactive messaging experience.

### Socket.io

Used for:

* Real-time messaging
* Chat events
* Call signaling
* Notifications
* Real-time application events

### WebRTC

Used for:

* Peer-to-peer audio communication
* Peer-to-peer video communication
* Real-time media streams

---

## Database

The application uses MongoDB for persistent data storage.

The backend contains models for:

* Users
* Messages
* Chats
* Status updates
* Calls

MongoDB Atlas can be used as the cloud-hosted database.

---

## Security

The application includes several security mechanisms:

* JWT authentication
* Protected API routes
* Authentication middleware
* Environment-based secrets
* Password authentication
* Server-side request validation

For production deployments, use strong secrets and HTTPS.

---

## Development

### Frontend

```bash
cd client
npm run dev
```

### Backend

```bash
cd server
npm run dev
```

Run both applications simultaneously during development.

---

## Production Build

Build the frontend using:

```bash
cd client
npm run build
```

The production files will be generated in the frontend build directory.

